## Human intervention needed

The automated job failed for `net.minidev:accessors-smart:2.4.3`. Preserved work is available at https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9361-fails-javac-compile-net.minidev-accessors-smart-2.4.3-4f020739.

The root cause is that Maven Central does not contain the main `accessors-smart-2.4.3.jar`. The initial compile failed with `Could not find accessors-smart-2.4.3.jar`. The preserved workaround compiles the published sources into a local JAR, allowing both JVM and Native Image tests to pass, but finalization still fails: `generateLibraryStats` reports `No eligible artifacts found on the classpath`. Dynamic-access coverage fails for the same reason. Metrics consequently report `failure`, 4 iterations, 0 generated/tested-library LOC, 0 metadata entries, and unavailable coverage.

